  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Continued rain through the weekend, with \nhighest amounts Downeast. The rainfall may provide some drought \nrelief.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nThe center of the low pressure system will progress NNE tonight\nand move through SE Maine. Heavier rain bands will also move N\nthroughout the night. By Sunday, the approaching ridge will\nbegin to move the low to the east. High-res models show a more\nshowery set up to the rain on the back end of the system, but\nupper air model soundings show a fairly moist column into the\nupper levels. Nevertheless, rain is likely throughout the\nmorning. By late afternoon, the rest of the rain will exit to\nthe NE.",
